&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own sourcing strategy across semiconductors and hardware, data center equipment, and energy equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the organization: develop the category leads and set how the teams operate as they grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Secure supply ahead of demand through capacity reservations, wafer commitments and long-term agreements, working with the rest of the Compute team as well as domain experts in Finance and Legal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold executive relationships with hardware suppliers and power and infrastructure OEMs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own supply risk, including single-source exposure, geography, tariffs and export controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify supply gaps before they impact the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 15+ years in strategic sourcing or supply chain for semiconductors, hardware, or datacenter infrastructure, and have led a function rather than a single category.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built a sourcing organization through rapid growth, including managers who lead teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have negotiated capacity or long-term supply agreements at multibillion-dollar scale with executive counterparts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have deep experience in either semiconductor supply (foundry, memory or hardware) or data center and power infrastructure equipment, and the judgment to lead the other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can make hard allocation calls and explain the trade-offs to executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have strong written communication and executive presence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
